      "subtopics": [
        {
          "title": "What each paragraph must do",
          "text": "<strong>Opening:</strong> state the post, the source of the advertisement and the reference number, so the letter reaches the right file. <strong>Body 1:</strong> your qualification plus the two or three skills the advertisement actually asked for. <strong>Body 2:</strong> proof — a project, an internship, a result. <strong>Close:</strong> ask for the interview, state your availability, thank them. Nothing else belongs in a cover letter."
        },
        {
          "title": "Solicited and unsolicited applications",
          "text": "A <strong>solicited</strong> application replies to an advertised vacancy, so it can quote the advertisement and match the stated requirements point by point. An <strong>unsolicited</strong> application is sent when no vacancy has been advertised; it must work harder — opening with why <em>that company</em> interests you, and asking to be considered for any suitable future opening."
