      "examAnswer": "Electronic mail, or email, is a method of exchanging written messages electronically over a computer network, and it has largely replaced the printed letter in business communication. Its advantages are speed, very low cost, the ability to reach recipients anywhere in the world at any time, the facility to attach documents, the ability to send a message to many recipients simultaneously, and the automatic creation of a searchable written record. Its limitations include the absence of tone and body language, dependence on internet access, the risks of spam, phishing and virus attacks, the fact that a message cannot be recalled once sent, and information overload. Email etiquette requires a clear and specific subject line, a proper salutation, short and well-organised paragraphs, correct use of the To, CC and BCC fields, avoidance of capital letters and SMS abbreviations, a professional sign-off with the sender's identity, and careful proofreading before sending.",
